                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/939: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-10T18:00:00-04:00">December 10, 1941—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>221. Department’s circular telegram December 8, 1 a.m. The Government feels that
                    use of communications facilities here in ways inimical to continental defense is
                    unlikely from practical standpoint but will give matter earnest attention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
